<type>[(scope)][!]: <short description>


# A semantic commit follows the [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) standard to automate versioning and changelogs. [1, 2] 
# ## Basic Structure
# 
# <type>[optional scope][!]: <description>
# 
# [optional body]
# 
# [optional footer(s)]
# 
# ------------------------------
# ## Commit Message Template
# 
# <type>(<scope>): <short description>
# 
# [optional longer body: explain "what" and "why", not "how"]
# 
# [optional footer: e.g., Fixes #123 or BREAKING CHANGE: description]
# 
# ------------------------------
# ## Common Commit Types
# 
# * feat: Introduces a new feature (correlates with a MINOR semantic version bump)
# * fix: Patches a bug (correlates with a PATCH semantic version bump)
# * docs: Documentation-only changes
# * style: Changes that do not affect code meaning (white-space, formatting, missing semi-colons)
# * refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# * perf: Code change that improves performance
# * test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# * build: Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies
# * ci: Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
# * chore: Other changes that don't modify src or test files
# * revert: Reverts a previous commit [1, 2, 3, 4] 
# 
# ------------------------------
# ## Breaking Changes
# 
# * Add an ! right before the colon (e.g., feat(api)!: drop v1 endpoints).
# * Or include a BREAKING CHANGE: footer in the commit body.
# * This triggers a MAJOR version bump in semantic versioning. [1, 2, 5] 
# 
# ------------------------------
# ## Examples
# Simple Feature:
# 
# feat(auth): add OAuth2 login button
# 
# Bug Fix with Issue Reference:
# 
# fix(parser): handle null pointer exception on empty input
# 
# Closes #402
# 
# Breaking Change:
# 
# refactor(api)!: remove deprecated user profile endpoints
# 
# BREAKING CHANGE: /api/v1/profile is removed; use /api/v2/profile instead.
# 
# 
# [1] [https://www.conventionalcommits.org](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)
# [2] [https://www.conventionalcommits.org](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0-beta.2/)
